{: #fig-flow title="Discovery Ecosystem Flow of Control" artwork-align="center"}

The flow starts at the agent resource on the right of the figure. It publishes its information to the agent
catalog and to a capabilities file if one is used.

Registration to the agent registry may be made direct by the agent resource or from the agent catalog.

The location of the agent catalog is advertised or discovered by other agents/users/clients. This step may form part of DAWN.

Any agent (on the left of the figure) can search the catalog to find a list of potential agent resources to communicate with. It may
cache the results, and selects one that it wishes to communicate with.

The agent then performs a discovery lookup to find the critical details necessary to communicate with the agent resource and the location of any
capabilities file that might exist for the agent resource. Again, the agent may cache the result. This step in the flow of control corresponds to 
DAWN.

The agent may read the capabilities file and decide to select a different agent resource, or to continue with the one first selected.

The agent then bootstraps its communications with the agent resource. This step may include an exchange of capabilities and potentially 
the negotiation of behaviors.

Finally, the agent is able to enter into full communication with the agent resource.

